+with a count legend. Only depicted heavy atoms are marked; this display does not infer a reaction
+or a unique atom mapping. **Enlarge 2D** docks the drawing in the right sidebar without moving
+the 3D camera; **Compact 2D** restores the floating panel. The chosen drawing size persists during
+checkpoint review. The `sos1-chemical-edits` registered story reproduces the paper's highlighted
+chemical sequence using only frozen checkpoint imports and display actions. See the
+[Figure 2 review and reproduction notes](paper/review/INTERFACE-CHEMISTRY-REVIEW-2026-09-07.md).
+
+`view.setDepictionAlignment({referenceSmarts, enabled:true})` uses the current strict
+2D drawing as a reference and constrains subsequent drawings to the requested shared
+SMARTS substructure (at least three atoms). This changes only 2D layout, not molecular
+bonds, stereochemistry, 3D coordinates, or camera settings. The human equivalent is
+**Scaffold alignment → Align** in the 2D panel. **Clear alignment**, or the same API
+action with `{enabled:false}`, removes the reference; clear it before loading an
+unrelated scaffold. A nonmatching structure reports an alignment error rather than
+silently claiming alignment. The `sos1-chemical-edits-aligned` display-only story
+uses eight shared scaffold atoms for the aligned Figure 2 revision.
+
 `view.setDisplay` also exposes the human-visible story palettes: `design-hit`,
 `design-prediction`, and `design-validation` render ligand carbons in saturated teal, purple, and
 orange respectively, while reducing ordinary pocket carbon and receptor-cartoon contrast. The
